===Etymology===
The [[#Adjective|adjective]] is first attested in the second part of the 15{{sup|th}} century, in {{w|Middle English}}, the [[#Verb|verb]] in 1538, the [[#Noun|noun]] in 1921; {{inh+|en|enm|saturat|saturat(e)|t=satiated, satisfied|nocap=1}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|saturātus}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|saturō|t=to fill, satisfy, quench}} (see {{m|en|-ate|pos=etymology 1, 2 and 3}}), from {{m|la|satur|t=full}} + {{m|la|-ō|id=denominative|pos=verb-forming suffix}}.

===Pronunciation===
