===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to become completely [[permeate]]d with, or [[soak]]ed (especially with a liquid).
#: {{syn|en|drench|impregnate|soak}}
#: {{ux|en|Rain '''saturated''' their clothes.}}
#: {{ux|en|After walking home in the driving rain, his clothes were '''saturated'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1815|journal=Annals of Philosophy|volume=6|page=332
|passage=Suppose, on the contrary, that a piece of charcoal '''saturated''' with hydrogen gas is put into a receiver filled with carbonic acid gas, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|chapter=12|passage=Innumerable flocks and herds covered that vast expanse of emerald meadow, '''saturated''' with the moisture of the Atlantic.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To fill thoroughly or to excess.
#: {{ux|en|Modern television is '''saturated''' with violence.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|chemistry}} To satisfy the affinity of; to cause a substance to become inert by chemical combination with all that it can hold.
#: {{ux|en|One can '''saturate''' phosphorus with chlorine.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|optics}} To render pure, or of a colour free from white light.

